<title>UK: BOE raises minimum lending rate 1/4 point to 6.0%.</title>
<headline>BOE raises minimum lending rate 1/4 point to 6.0%.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said on Wednesday it had raised the minimum lending rate by a quarter-point to 6.0 percent.  </p>
<p>The Bank bought 14 million stg in band one bank bills at 5-15/16 percent, signalling a quarter-point increase in interest rates.</p>
</text>
